# Cloudflare Pages _redirects
#
# Goals (root cause of GSC "duplicate without user-selected canonical" on
# 2026-05-10 was that every random URL returned HTTP 200 + the homepage HTML):
#   1. Send the common "phantom" URLs to their correct destinations with 301s
#      so any already-indexed bad URLs flow link equity to the right page.
#   2. Everything else 404s via the catchall — Astro builds 404.html from
#      src/pages/404.astro.
#
# CF Pages evaluates rules top-to-bottom; first match wins. Specific rules
# MUST come before the /* catchall. No "!" suffix here because none of these
# from-paths conflict with built static files, so default precedence is fine.

# Phantom marketing URLs that were getting indexed as duplicate-homepage
/download    https://login.quickztna.com/download    301
/install     https://login.quickztna.com/install     301
/signin      https://login.quickztna.com/auth        301
/signup      https://login.quickztna.com/auth        301
/login       https://login.quickztna.com/auth        301
/auth        https://login.quickztna.com/auth        301
/dashboard   https://login.quickztna.com/            301
/admin       https://login.quickztna.com/            301

# Section-level redirects (people guess these)
/sso         /docs/integrations/                     301
/api         /docs/api/                              301
/cli         /docs/cli/                              301
/security    /docs/security/                         301
/quickstart  /guide/quickstart/                      301
/install.sh  https://login.quickztna.com/install.sh  301
/install.ps1 https://login.quickztna.com/install.ps1 301

# Legacy old-docs paths if anyone tries the pre-2026-05-16 structure on apex
/docs/quickstart        /guide/quickstart/   301
/docs/getting-started   /guide/              301

# Always serve /sitemap.xml — many crawlers default to this path before they
# look at robots.txt for the actual sitemap reference. Mirror to sitemap-index.xml.
/sitemap.xml /sitemap-index.xml                    200

# Deleted 2026-06-02 — these two PQC posts made product claims the shipped
# product cannot back. Redirect to the blog index so any inbound link,
# bookmark, or SERP click lands somewhere coherent instead of a 404. CF
# edge cache (s-maxage=604800) may continue serving the old HTML for up
# to 7 days for cache-warm URLs.
/blog/post-quantum-free-tier-manifesto/  /blog/    301
/blog/only-pqc-ready-ztna-solution-2026/ /blog/    301

# Everything else (real 404, not duplicate-home 200)
/*           /404.html                              404
